# Project left-nav drag reorder

## Goal

Users can reorder Projects by dragging in the expanded left-most nav (`AppNav`). DnD UI exists **only** there. Order is persisted and returned by `GET /api/v1/projects`.

## Branch

`phase-project-nav-reorder`

## Backend

1. Add `projects.sort_order` (not null, default 0).
2. Migration backfills existing rows to `0..n-1` by current `updated_at DESC`.
3. `GET /` orders by `sortOrder`, `id`.
4. `POST /` appends with `max(sortOrder) + 1`.
5. `PATCH /reorder` with `{ orderedProjectIds }` before `/:id` routes.
6. Update `docs/database/`; sync schema docs after migrate.

## Frontend

1. `@dnd-kit` sortable project rows in expanded AppNav only.
2. “All projects” / “New project” stay outside the sortable set.
3. Optimistic React Query cache update + PATCH reorder; invalidate on failure.

## Out of scope

- DnD on All projects grid or other nav sections.
- Status grouping / pinning.
- Single-entity PATCH `sortOrder`.
